mantle rm377
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_oda_kelpworth
title the smoke-mapped mane
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=herder
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sketches_a_walk_in_smoky_dust_on_a_grooming_board
likes plum_tart long_walks old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes early_bells stale_bread
fears a_tired_beast_missing_a_turn
hopes to_map_a_long_gentle_walk
topics animals +0.5 travel +0.3 family +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=close refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# traces routes in the dust on a grooming board and rubs each map away before putting the brushes by.

words
oath! = Brush my compass sideways | By the long currycomb
saying! = A map can travel on a brush back | Leave the steep way to the eager feet
board = a dusty brush board | my wooden grooming tray
comb = the blunt currycomb | a little horn comb
dust = a smoke-grey drift | a soft layer of dust
lane = my finger-wide lane | a road drawn in dust
turn = a faint hooked turn | the curve on my map
plum = a dark plum half | a wedge of purple fruit
tart = my pie corner | a warm tart slice
frost = a white saddle of rime | a crust of hoarfrost
strap = the worn head strap | a broad webbing strap
hoof = a broad hoof mark | a clear half moon
rag = my bridle rag | a short dry cloth
bell = the first unwanted clang | a rude waking bell

any
opinion festivals for 3 : A good dance costs about as much room as grooming a horse and does wonders for one's opinion of both feet.
opinion houses against 1 : I'd like the paws that own the fine stables to come and see where the long walk starts.
opinion merchants against 1 : A little dust drawn over the old price doesn't keep me from remembering yesterday's figure.
opinion strangers against 1 : I watch an unfamiliar wolf round the beasts for a while. A smooth voice alone doesn't settle a skittish head.
opinion road mixed 0 : A road looks different to a beast on sore feet. I won't judge the whole journey from a dry seat.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You've come along a new turning. Welcome. | Mind the brushes. My greetings are cleaner.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I can free the dustier paw for you. | Stand where both my eyes can find you.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The map's still a blank board. | Clean frost or clean dust, I'm ready for company.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The lines look soft now. | Step into the last pale margin.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin travel right across my borders. | A familiar set of feet on my road.
line again.open : Round my little map a second time. | The turning's brought you back to me.
line greet.return : Heard and marked clearly. | Allow me a quick brush of the cuff.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I can trace that footstep without looking. | Your face gets a comfortable place on my map.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One ear's on the brushes. One's on you. | Let me lay the comb flat first.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Your stride's quite distinct. | My ears navigate better after dark.
line farewell : Good ground all four corners of the way. | Take the turn with the gentler slope.
line farewell.return : I'll keep my thumb on the route. | May the dust settle kindly behind you.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Easy hoof marks under lamplight. | Look for the quiet gate home.
line react.news : Draw me the outline of it. | Where does the account turn?
line react.news.new : An unmarked road for me. | Fresh dust on my map.
line react.news.known : I've traced that particular route already. | A familiar bend in the tale.
line react.news.doubt : I'd see whether the second turning really joins the first. | That account covers a surprising distance on very few footsteps.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's a hard mile you've brought in. | Hush awhile. I'll keep my hand steady.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A fine open way ahead, by that account. | I'm pleased to find a bright turning.
line ask.how : How has the going been underfoot? | Which part of your day's rubbed sore?
line answer.how : Mostly on the gentle track today. | Got dust enough left for another little road.
line decline : I'd sooner take a quieter path this time. | I must save a little walking strength for another duty.
line accept_decline : Your feet can choose their turning. | Fair. Neither of us needs the extra miles.
line thank : That saves me some hard going. | I'll mark that kindness on the clean side.
line sympathise : Share the sheltered part of my road. | Walk by me with the sore foot inboard.
line reassure : One short stretch and a pause is plenty. | No use drawing the whole mile just yet.
line preclose : I'll clear the board for the next errand. | Time to put the combs by.

scene map
when topic=work self.job=herder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw routes on #board# with the tip of the comb.
b : For a beast to read? | How long do they last?
a : For me to remember where a tired beast doesn't want to turn. | One good wipe. By then I ought to have the route between my ears.

scene smoke
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My coat keeps a faint smell of smoke even with a clean brush.
b : A smoky brush? | Does it bother the beasts?
a : Smoke's on me. The brush is more willing to be improved. | Not if I stop a little way off and let a nose examine the subject first.

scene tart
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plum tart stains the tip of the finger I draw maps with.
b : A purple road? | Is that any use?
a : Beautifully definite. Much too delicious to be permanent. | If there's a lost spot of jam I can consult my own finger for directions.

scene walk
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long walk agrees with me better if there's one entirely unnecessary bend.
b : Why unnecessary? | Don't you get tired?
a : A necessary one belongs to the errand. I want a turn of my own. | I pick a bend round level ground. I'm fanciful with some discretion.

scene oldmap
when topic=travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a map old enough to leave a gate where a wall stands now.
b : Of what use? | Would you mend it?
a : It tells me where tired feet once expected an opening. | In dust, yes. In ink I'd keep both versions of that street.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rime on a stable latch shows exactly which paw was there first.
b : Does it hurt to open? | Useful information?
a : I wrap my cuff round it. Only my sleeve complains afterwards. | Enough to know I haven't left a beast waiting for a first look.

scene bell
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I object to early bells on behalf of all creatures with ears.
b : The whole lot? | Do you sleep through any?
a : Let each protest in the customary voice. I can manage the wolf's part. | Not once the bell has opened formal proceedings against sleep.

scene stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I soak old bread before I can be tempted to call it a biscuit.
b : Will that save it? | What do you soak it in?
a : It'll save my jaw. The bread wasn't choosing the matter. | A spoon of warm milk when I have it. Water works without the compliment.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could draw the route home to #self.spouse# with my eyes closed.
b : Is that a promise? | How would you know the last turn?
a : It's a pleasure. Nobody's asking me to do it blind in the street. | A hand knows where to turn when there's a welcome at the far end.

scene memory
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wharf whistle can make me wish every route had a gentler turning.
b : Someone you miss? | Do you go down there much?
a : There's a place my memory walks to of its own accord. I'll keep it private. | When I need to. I don't spend my leisure looking for a hard mile.

scene horses
when topic=work self.job=herder self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I put a hand near a nose before so much as lifting the strap.
b : One sniff enough? | Why your hand first?
a : A sniff and a little time to look. I don't like my own surprises forced on me either. | Because a strap hasn't much of an introduction in it.

scene estate
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Estate keeps an admirable quantity of gate in the way of a simple walk.
b : Who's allowed through? | How do you manage?
a : That can take longer to discover than the walk itself. | Learn the polite open turns. There are still a few.

scene marketprices
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge the price of a brush by the hairs left behind after one pass.
b : Fewer is better? | Could you test that at a stall?
a : If they belong to the brush, certainly. Dirt ought to be more easily parted from its home. | On my own sleeve. It's generally dusty enough for commerce.

scene known
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather introduce a newcomer to the head end first.
b : Of a horse? | What about introductions to wolves?
a : Yes. The back end has a limited choice of greetings. | Same principle. Let both parties see whom they're dealing with.

scene mood
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If #self.friend# wanted quiet I'd draw a whole walk in dust without a word.
b : Do you need a compass? | Would the walk be a long one?
a : The only north that matters is where the person opposite wants to look. | Just long enough to get us both thinking of something pleasant.

scene muck
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The road under a hoof can look dry and feel quite wrong.
b : Can you tell before stepping? | What's your usual clue?
a : Sometimes. I test a doubtful bit with the hard tip of my shoe. | A little shine along the rut where water's sitting below the crust.

scene feast
when topic=festival self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm partial to festivals on account of a particular wedding dance.
b : Your own? | How long ago?
a : My feet were certainly present. I recall them making very grand claims on the floor. | Long enough to remember the tune and forget every unsteady step.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed my map turned into a mane that needed combing from both ends.
b : Which end did you choose? | How did you find home?
a : The tail end of the road. The beginning was too badly tangled. | My finger followed a clear parting straight up to the gate.

story plummap [topic=food]
  : I drew a map in plum juice once. There was a perfectly dignified road round the rim of the plate and a large red crossroads near the centre.
  : I turned the plate to make the directions clear. The crossroads moved downhill to meet the road and the entire district became a puddle.
  b : Could you save the route?
  : Of course. I ate the rest of the tart and took the long way home.

story saddle [topic=work self.job=herder]
  : Once I cleaned a saddle strap so thoroughly that one short length gleamed like water. I could see the stable lamp reflected in it as I worked.
  : I kept rubbing at a spot in the reflection, thinking the strap was still dirty. Then I moved my head and the spot moved too.
  b : A mark on your face?
  : A smut by my nose. After that I gave some attention to cleaning the groom as well as the gear.

story drawnwalk [topic=travel]
  : I used a quick map to show myself a new route. It began on the grooming board and continued up the wooden handle of a brush where I ran out of space.
  : I picked up the brush to follow the route with a finger. The important turning was now in my palm and half my road drifted to the floor.
  b : Did you find the place?
  : Next day. I left the brush down the second time and wrote the tricky turn inside my own cuff.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=herder self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Let the nose have first acquaintance with the brush. | Draw the wide turning before the narrow gate.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Purple finger. Fine weather for drawing a road. | Save the clean crust for the walk.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rime on the latch, dry cuff on my hand. | Tea before the bell gets a second opinion.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.dislikes=stale_bread
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Give that heel a little softening. | Old crust needs a gentle approach too.

dlg resident.hub : Choose a corner that affords a view of the board. I've just room to draw whatever turning's troubling you.
dlg resident.job [self.job=herder self.workplace] : I look after the beasts at #self.workplace#. They have clear opinions about the difference between a road and a proper walk.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This is where the present account leads. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've a familiar footfall to add to my dust map.
dlg resident.bye : Find yourself an unnecessary turning worth walking for.

graft resident.hub
choice Show me the kind way round on your map. -> kind_route
node kind_route
say This line runs straight up a steep bank. Draw your thumb along it and there's a knot under the dust. My other line goes round. A tired hoof would choose it.
free
choice Why keep the steep one at all? -> steep_saved
choice I can feel the slope in the board. -> hub
node steep_saved
say For the young feet that enjoy climbing. A kind road doesn't have to be the same shape for every traveller.
choice I'll take the short climb today. -> hub
choice I'm finding the level route. -> bye
